WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:02.435
- And we unfortunately
live now in this culture

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.107
that almost glorifies failure.

00:00:04.107 --> 00:00:06.845
Like, we're supposed to
be so happy, oh fail fast.

00:00:06.845 --> 00:00:08.935
The average multi-millionaire in the US

00:00:08.935 --> 00:00:11.874
has seven different sources of income.

00:00:11.874 --> 00:00:14.119
No life will ever be
saved by you responding

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:15.765
to someone who's negative to you.

00:00:15.765 --> 00:00:17.684
If you help a million people,
you'll make a million dollars.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.381
The city I'm going to is
so amazing and wonderful,

00:00:20.381 --> 00:00:23.406
that everyone else wants to
be here even faster than me.

00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:25.493
Warner Brothers, we did
all the movie studios that

00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:26.980
were based in New York, we did all

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.443
the record labels based in New York.

00:00:28.443 --> 00:00:30.299
We all have to decide for ourselves

00:00:30.299 --> 00:00:32.443
what our individual dream is.

00:00:32.443 --> 00:00:34.674
Because I know, you're all
going to write to me and say,

00:00:34.674 --> 00:00:36.850
"I can't believe, my brain's

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.001
"like Bradley Cooper in Limitless now."

00:00:39.001 --> 00:00:41.117
If you don't make the
choices in your own life,

00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:44.855
then someone else is going to
end up making them for you.

00:00:44.855 --> 00:00:47.015
So, I'm good at the writing part.

00:00:47.015 --> 00:00:49.277
I don't know how to design a hardcover.

00:00:49.277 --> 00:00:51.450
- He's an American hedge fund manager,

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.163
entrepreneur, and author.

00:00:53.163 --> 00:00:55.832
He's founded or co-founded
more than 20 companies.

00:00:55.832 --> 00:00:58.644
USA Today named his book, Choose Yourself,

00:00:58.644 --> 00:01:02.010
as one of the top 12
business books of all time.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.758
He's James Altucher, and here are

00:01:03.758 --> 00:01:05.531
his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.864
(swooshing)

00:01:08.853 --> 00:01:11.950
- I had failed and succeeded and failed.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.676
I had started over 20
businesses, 17 of them failed.

00:01:14.676 --> 00:01:16.930
And we unfortunately live now in this

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.919
culture that almost glorifies failure.

00:01:18.919 --> 00:01:21.582
Like we're supposed to be
so happy, oh fail fast.

00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:24.074
It's like this failure pornography almost.

00:01:24.074 --> 00:01:25.381
(audience laughs)

00:01:25.381 --> 00:01:28.587
We just worship people who
fail and then somehow succeed.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:31.063
But I can tell you that
failure is really unpleasant,

00:01:31.063 --> 00:01:35.146
and it's much better to
view it as an experiment.

00:01:37.249 --> 00:01:41.456
Thomas Edison, he didn't fail 10,000 times

00:01:41.456 --> 00:01:43.686
when he was making an electric light bulb,

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:45.186
he just experimented, and then

00:01:45.186 --> 00:01:46.289
he made an electric light bulb.

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:48.470
We don't consider that the
guy was lying on the street

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.487
about to kill himself
on the every first try.

00:01:50.487 --> 00:01:52.313
(audience laughs)
He tried 10,000 times.

00:01:52.313 --> 00:01:53.734
Always have a plan B.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.036
Remember, and this is all census data,

00:01:56.036 --> 00:01:58.443
the average multimillionaire I the US

00:01:58.443 --> 00:02:01.242
has seven different sources of income.

00:02:01.242 --> 00:02:04.974
So that means they have
plan Bs all the time.

00:02:04.974 --> 00:02:06.638
There's never a question,
"OK, that's not working."

00:02:06.638 --> 00:02:10.089
I had a business that I invested in,

00:02:10.089 --> 00:02:12.828
a lot of money recently,
and it wasn't working.

00:02:12.828 --> 00:02:15.286
But I have plan Bs, like
seven other plan Bs.

00:02:15.286 --> 00:02:19.705
So I'm able to say, "OK,
this is bringing me down

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.408
"every time I talk to you guys.

00:02:21.408 --> 00:02:22.869
"I'm not going to talk to you anymore

00:02:22.869 --> 00:02:25.081
"unless you have something
good to say to me."

00:02:25.081 --> 00:02:28.199
And they could kick and scream,

00:02:28.199 --> 00:02:29.567
"But you put all this money in!"

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:32.982
I'm like, "OK, I'm done
with that, I have plan Bs."

00:02:32.982 --> 00:02:35.885
So all the time think
about how many plan Bs.

00:02:35.885 --> 00:02:38.300
Notice when I had a job
at HBO, I had a plan B.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.262
Before I left my job at HBO,

00:02:41.262 --> 00:02:43.260
I had my company running on the side

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.393
for 18 months before I left full-time.

00:02:46.393 --> 00:02:47.912
I had a dozen employees at my company.

00:02:47.912 --> 00:02:50.735
So always have the plan Bs.

00:02:50.735 --> 00:02:54.080
And then it's easy to leave
early in every situation.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.951
Now again, you don't have
plan Bs in relationships.

00:02:55.951 --> 00:02:58.132
There's other things there
you have to be careful of.

00:02:58.132 --> 00:02:59.298
(audience laughs)

00:02:59.298 --> 00:03:02.131
But you know, that's another talk.

00:03:03.886 --> 00:03:07.230
You really can't be
around negative people,

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:08.671
or people that are going to put you down.

00:03:08.671 --> 00:03:09.974
Who's going to put you down?

00:03:09.974 --> 00:03:13.584
It's not the neighbor down
the street, it's your mother.

00:03:13.584 --> 00:03:16.242
(audience laughs)
It's true.

00:03:16.242 --> 00:03:20.018
Or it's your friend or your colleague.

00:03:20.018 --> 00:03:23.398
And if they want to engage
with you in the negativity,

00:03:23.398 --> 00:03:24.746
you can't argue with them.

00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:26.364
You're like, "OK, I hear you,

00:03:26.364 --> 00:03:29.354
I'm going to eat my
food now," or whatever.

00:03:29.354 --> 00:03:32.271
It's like for instance, I see this,

00:03:33.356 --> 00:03:35.732
I did a Reddit yesterday, a Reddit AMA,

00:03:35.732 --> 00:03:37.361
you know one of those
things that's a Q&amp;A thing.

00:03:37.361 --> 00:03:40.144
And you see all the
time, people are trying

00:03:40.144 --> 00:03:42.682
to say negative stuff
just to get you sucked in.

00:03:42.682 --> 00:03:44.323
You see it on the internet all the time.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:45.576
They call it internet trolls.

00:03:45.576 --> 00:03:48.507
You never ever respond to any of that.

00:03:48.507 --> 00:03:51.803
Nothing ever good, no
life will ever be saved

00:03:51.803 --> 00:03:54.331
by you responding to someone
who's negative to you.

00:03:54.331 --> 00:03:56.681
So this is very important,
and the next step

00:03:56.681 --> 00:03:58.754
is obviously surround
yourself with completely

00:03:58.754 --> 00:04:00.655
positive people who are inspiring to you,

00:04:00.655 --> 00:04:02.864
who are supportive of you.
That works very well.

00:04:02.864 --> 00:04:05.657
You need to have some
meaning in your life,

00:04:05.657 --> 00:04:08.482
so it's meaning in your
life that causes you

00:04:08.482 --> 00:04:11.106
to have idea that will help people.

00:04:11.106 --> 00:04:13.202
And that's how you create.

00:04:13.202 --> 00:04:14.876
There's a saying, "If you
help a million people,

00:04:14.876 --> 00:04:15.932
you'll make a million dollars."

00:04:15.932 --> 00:04:20.647
So the dollars is like the
side effect of helping people.

00:04:20.647 --> 00:04:22.189
First people have to be helped.

00:04:22.189 --> 00:04:23.928
Then that means first you have to be

00:04:23.928 --> 00:04:25.519
really good at coming up with ideas.

00:04:25.519 --> 00:04:27.704
So I always say you have
to have this idea muscle

00:04:27.704 --> 00:04:31.871
that you exercise regularly,
so you're an idea machine,

00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:37.787
so that you can then help people,

00:04:37.787 --> 00:04:40.437
which then in turn helps you
figure out how to make money.

00:04:40.437 --> 00:04:42.385
Or you don't even have to
figure it out at that point.

00:04:42.385 --> 00:04:43.660
You'll make money.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.787
Waking up every morning and figuring out,

00:04:45.787 --> 00:04:47.539
even in a difficult situation,

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:49.647
where the pieces of gratitude are.

00:04:49.647 --> 00:04:53.427
So coming into this city
yesterday or the day before,

00:04:53.427 --> 00:04:56.332
I was stuck in traffic, and
I was late for something,

00:04:56.332 --> 00:04:58.028
and I was like, "Ugh,
you got to go faster!"

00:04:58.028 --> 00:05:00.894
But this is opportunity to solve

00:05:00.894 --> 00:05:03.604
a difficult gratitude problem, which is,

00:05:03.604 --> 00:05:07.222
the city I'm going to is
so amazing and wonderful,

00:05:07.222 --> 00:05:10.763
that everyone else wants to
be here even faster than me.

00:05:10.763 --> 00:05:13.235
So I'm grateful to be
going into this city.

00:05:13.235 --> 00:05:15.137
There were similarities between

00:05:15.137 --> 00:05:17.310
all these types of sales, which is,

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.371
you get someone to say, you give,

00:05:20.371 --> 00:05:23.755
then you get someone to say
yes, so your foot's in the door.

00:05:23.755 --> 00:05:25.756
You do anything you can to get the yes.

00:05:25.756 --> 00:05:28.693
And then I would always over-deliver.

00:05:28.693 --> 00:05:30.061
I kind of left this part out.

00:05:30.061 --> 00:05:32.440
I would always over-deliver,
at least initially.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.984
I would work so hard to over-deliver.

00:05:34.984 --> 00:05:36.729
Just do something that they didn't expect.

00:05:36.729 --> 00:05:38.608
So for instance, I'll just tell you,

00:05:38.608 --> 00:05:41.108
on Stockpicker, as an example,

00:05:43.144 --> 00:05:44.976
the day the deal was announced,

00:05:44.976 --> 00:05:47.225
the day that we officially
launched our partnership,

00:05:47.225 --> 00:05:50.405
I released a whole new section of the site

00:05:50.405 --> 00:05:53.354
that they weren't even
expecting, which was a Q&amp;A.

00:05:53.354 --> 00:05:57.521
Kind of like a Quora-like
sub-site within the site.

00:05:58.376 --> 00:06:01.682
And that doubled our
traffic almost overnight.

00:06:01.682 --> 00:06:03.379
They were completely not expecting it.

00:06:03.379 --> 00:06:05.042
So I always made an attempt,

00:06:05.042 --> 00:06:07.000
when I was first building a relationship,

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.954
and all through the relationship really,

00:06:08.954 --> 00:06:10.639
but it's easiest to do when you're first

00:06:10.639 --> 00:06:13.476
building the relationship,
is to surprise and delight.

00:06:13.476 --> 00:06:15.686
Always give extra services.

00:06:15.686 --> 00:06:17.664
When I was in the web
design business in the 90s,

00:06:17.664 --> 00:06:21.831
we did miramax.com, New Line,
Fine Line, Warner Brothers.

00:06:24.352 --> 00:06:26.510
We did all the movie studios
that were based in New York.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.583
We did all the record
labels based in New York.

00:06:28.583 --> 00:06:31.941
So we were, our sector was
the entertainment industry.

00:06:31.941 --> 00:06:35.591
No matter what, we always over-delivered

00:06:35.591 --> 00:06:37.080
on every site that we spec'd out,

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.293
every time that we had
a meeting with a client,

00:06:39.293 --> 00:06:40.716
there was always extra things.

00:06:40.716 --> 00:06:43.242
Nobody could ever complain,
"This isn't what we asked for,"

00:06:43.242 --> 00:06:45.035
because we always delivered more.

00:06:45.035 --> 00:06:49.780
So that was an important part
of being a trusted source,

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.625
so that people would continue to use

00:06:51.625 --> 00:06:53.099
our services on the next sites.

00:06:53.099 --> 00:06:55.016
We all have to decide for ourselves

00:06:55.016 --> 00:06:57.124
what our individual dream is.

00:06:57.124 --> 00:07:00.707
Don't subscribe to some
mass hypnosis dream

00:07:01.776 --> 00:07:05.806
that was designed to get
us to spend as much money

00:07:05.806 --> 00:07:09.739
and time on other people's
dreams as possible.

00:07:09.739 --> 00:07:13.423
Choose your own dream
and follow that first.

00:07:13.423 --> 00:07:15.765
Writing down these 10 ideas a day,

00:07:15.765 --> 00:07:18.982
if you do it for three months,
just try it for three months.

00:07:18.982 --> 00:07:20.534
You don't have to try it after that,

00:07:20.534 --> 00:07:22.838
because I know you're all
going to write to me and say,

00:07:22.838 --> 00:07:24.527
"I can't believe, my brain's

00:07:24.527 --> 00:07:26.595
"like Bradley Cooper in Limitless now.

00:07:26.595 --> 00:07:28.111
"I can't believe what happened

00:07:28.111 --> 00:07:30.735
"now that I'm writing
10 ideas a day down."

00:07:30.735 --> 00:07:33.085
We all the time have many choices in life.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.668
A great and wise man once said,

00:07:37.455 --> 00:07:40.286
"If you don't make the
choices in your own life,

00:07:40.286 --> 00:07:42.646
"then someone else is going to end up

00:07:42.646 --> 00:07:45.343
"making them for you,
and it won't be good."

00:07:45.343 --> 00:07:47.617
It might be a boss, it
might be a professor,

00:07:47.617 --> 00:07:49.913
it might be your parents, it might

00:07:49.913 --> 00:07:52.261
be colleagues, might be a company.

00:07:52.261 --> 00:07:54.096
Someone else is going to
start making choices for you,

00:07:54.096 --> 00:07:55.497
and they're not going to be as good

00:07:55.497 --> 00:07:57.950
as the choices you could make yourself.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.151
Of course, that great
and wise man was myself.

00:08:00.151 --> 00:08:01.425
Being very humble here.

00:08:01.425 --> 00:08:03.774
How do you execute, basically?
- (audience member) Yeah.

00:08:03.774 --> 00:08:07.671
- So it's like, your
brother, you have a team.

00:08:07.671 --> 00:08:10.028
You have people who help you.

00:08:10.028 --> 00:08:11.670
You know this as well as I do.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:13.411
I just had a book come out Monday.

00:08:13.411 --> 00:08:15.654
I'm good at the writing part.

00:08:15.654 --> 00:08:17.704
I don't know how to design a hardcover,

00:08:17.704 --> 00:08:20.594
I don't know how to do
the interior design,

00:08:20.594 --> 00:08:22.720
I'm not actually that good at
picking the title of a book.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.387
I'm not that great at marketing.

00:08:27.843 --> 00:08:29.798
I didn't know how to make an audiobook.

00:08:29.798 --> 00:08:31.717
I didn't know how to do anything.

00:08:31.717 --> 00:08:34.111
So I outsourced every
single piece of that.

00:08:34.111 --> 00:08:36.962
And by the way, I also got a pre-order

00:08:36.962 --> 00:08:40.189
of 5,000 copies of the hardcover

00:08:40.189 --> 00:08:43.743
to completely pay for all of
the expenses I had on the book.

00:08:43.743 --> 00:08:47.237
So the book itself to
publish it, I self-published,

00:08:47.237 --> 00:08:49.086
cost $30,000, give or take.

00:08:49.086 --> 00:08:51.790
I completely pre-ordered
to get more than that,

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:55.403
and then on top of that I've
also made more than that

00:08:55.403 --> 00:08:56.928
just from the marketing that I outsourced.

00:08:56.928 --> 00:09:00.178
To Mr. Ryan Holiday, who you know well.

00:09:01.403 --> 00:09:02.427
Does that answer...?
- Yes.

00:09:02.427 --> 00:09:03.260
(swooshing)

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:04.361
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:04.361 --> 00:09:07.363
I made this video because
Malik Sooch asked me to.

00:09:07.363 --> 00:09:08.958
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:09:08.958 --> 00:09:10.198
that you want me to profile next,

00:09:10.198 --> 00:09:12.647
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:09:12.647 --> 00:09:14.485
I'd also love to know which
of James's top 10 rules

00:09:14.485 --> 00:09:16.660
meant the most to you, will have

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.309
the biggest impact on
your life or business.

00:09:18.309 --> 00:09:20.150
Leave it in the comments below
and I'll join the discussion.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.464
And my personal goal with this channel

00:09:22.464 --> 00:09:23.538
is to hit a million subscribers,

00:09:23.538 --> 00:09:25.740
so anything you can think of to share it,

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.803
let people know about
it, spread this video,

00:09:27.803 --> 00:09:29.596
I'd really appreciate it.

00:09:29.596 --> 00:09:31.441
Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:31.441 --> 00:09:34.690
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:36.942
(swooshing)

